  "exact_novelty_delta": "This is the first written explicit construction found in this bounded screen that answers AT §6: s_k = k^(1/n) z_k/|z_k|, with z_k running through Z^n∖{0} in order of length. The contribution is the observation that ranking any lattice by length and placing the k-th point at radius k^(1/n) moves each point by o(1), because the ball-count error is o(R^(n−1)). Delone, density and uniform distribution then follow from standard facts. Priority is not established: search misses do not prove novelty, and the HDR PDF and Berestovskii full text are unread.",
