The separate classical audit read **Marklof**, “Delone sets generated by square roots,” [arXiv:2003.08319v1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.08319), all five pages: Proposition 1 gives the planar density/angular-distribution equivalence, and Proposition 3 gives a particular planar square-root-angle spiral. It also read the introduction/theorem statements and §4 of **Akiyama**, “Spiral Delone sets and three distance theorem,” [arXiv:1904.10815v2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.10815). Neither inspected text supplies the proposed all-dimensional norm-ranked construction.

MathOverflow discussions [145963](https://mathoverflow.net/questions/145963), [146398](https://mathoverflow.net/questions/146398), and [302348](https://mathoverflow.net/questions/302348) were read by that audit. They concern increasing-radius lattice walks, lattice-free radial gaps and thin spherical shells, respectively. No exact-radius rank-rescaling solution to this target was located there; these are discussion sources, not refereed papers.

