evidence/ForestSota.md:53:    {"claim": "Neither the arXiv math sweep nor the OpenAlex full-text sweep found a spiral-forest work beyond AT22, Tevet and Kashkan's thesis.", "quote": "math-category hits: 2506.22863, 2303.14719, 2111.02773, 2111.01843, 2010.06756, 1907.03501, 1406.3807 (plus non-math false positives)", "url": "http://export.arxiv.org/api/query?search_query=(abs:%22dense%20forest%22%20OR%20abs:%22dense%20forests%22%20OR%20ti:%22dense%20forest%22%20OR%20ti:%22dense%20forests%22)%20AND%20(cat:math.MG%20OR%20cat:math.NT%20OR%20cat:math.CO%20OR%20cat:math.DS%20OR%20cat:math.PR%20OR%20cat:math.CA%20OR%20cat:math.GT%20OR%20cat:math.MP)&sortBy=submittedDate&sortOrder=descending&max_results=40 ; https://api.openalex.org/works?filter=fulltext.search:%22dense%20forest%22,publication_year:2022-2026&search=spiral&select=id,title,doi,publication_date&per-page=50", "source": "arXiv API; OpenAlex full-text search", "date": "2026-10-14 accessed", "kind": "index queries", "verified": true, "stance": "nuance", "scope": "bounded screen"},
evidence/ForestSota.md:58:      "existence": "No spiral dense forest known. AT22 (v2 p.6): open, with a conjecture that none exists. Tevet (p.12): conjectures existence. Kashkan thesis (2025): unknown.",
evidence/ForestSota.md:70:      "Not gained: any visibility rate; uniform discreteness or Delone property (S is not uniformly discrete, because Z^2 + QZ^2 is dense in R^2 [INFERENCE, argued from no common rational direction]); a Danzer spiral; d ≥ 2 (the higher-dimensional AT22 case would follow by the same method using Shirandami's grids and Hlawka's discrepancy bound [INFERENCE, not in package]); 'natural' or phyllotactic spirals; anything about cone energy."
evidence/ForestSota.md:72:    "quantitative_note_INFERENCE": "The package's stability lemma gives V_S(eps) ≤ 2 V_A(eps/4) + 2 R(eps/4) + 4, where R(delta) is of order delta^-3 under the O(R^(2/3)) bound. With an explicit-rate base this yields roughly O(eps^-3) (Peres/ASW) or O(eps^-(5+eta)) for a uniformly discrete Delone spiral (ASW Thm 1.3). That is far from the O(eps^-1 ln eps^-1) frontier. Random bases (Alon, Kashkan) have radial count fluctuations of order r, so the vanishing-displacement transfer does not apply to them directly. None of this is proved in the package."
evidence/ForestSota.md:77:    {"result": "Adiceam 2016: O(eps^-2(d-1)-eta)", "source": "Kashkan v3 §1"},
evidence/ForestSota.md:80:    {"result": "Kashkan 2025: O(eps^-1 ln eps^-1), probabilistic, finite density", "source": "Kashkan v3 Thm 1.1"},
evidence/ForestSota.md:81:    {"result": "O(eps^-1) is equivalent to Danzer's problem and remains open", "source": "AT22 p.4; Alon §3; Kashkan v3 §1"},
evidence/ForestSota.md:87:    "would_upgrade": "An explicit near-optimal visibility rate for some spiral; a uniformly discrete (Delone) spiral forest with an explicit rate; a dynamically natural spiral (for example u_n = e(f(n)) with smooth f) that is a forest; a Danzer spiral set; all dimensions together with a human referee and a priority check."
evidence/ForestSota.md:92:    "The publisher full texts of Tevet (CNT 2025) and AT22 (Moscow J 2022) were not inspected because they are paywalled. Equivalence to arXiv v2 is inferred from milestones and the Crossref reference list.",
